{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Fin","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytAdjacentSwap","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytEntryMono","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytMathlibBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PermInversion","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtFinrankWired","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finite","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Free","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Basic"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_data_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_data_step","kind":"theorem","line":735,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L735-L828","doc":"**Seminormal transport along an admissible adjacent swap (sorry-free).** If a nonzero\n`v ∈ S^λ` is a simultaneous JM eigenvector with the content tuple of `T`, and\n`AdjacentSwapStep μ T T'`, then `w = ρ(s)·v − (c_b − c_a)⁻¹ • v` (with `s = (a, a+1)` and\n`c_a, c_b` the contents of `a, a+1` in `T`) is a nonzero simultaneous JM eigenvector in `S^λ`\nwith the content tuple of `T'`.\n\nThis is the classical induction step of Young's seminormal form, machine-checked end-to-end:\n* the JM recursion `s·X_a·s = X_b − s` / `s·X_m·s = X_m` (`conj_jucysMurphy_self` /\n  `conj_jucysMurphy_other`) is pushed through `asAlgebraHom` to `Module.End`;\n* the eigenvalue swap is `end_conj_shift_eigenvector_pair`, the fixed operators are\n  `end_conj_fix_eigenvector`, non-vanishing is `end_involution_eigenvector_ne`\n  (using `d ≠ 0`, `d² ≠ 1` cast into `k` by `CharZero`);\n* membership is the subrepresentation property `rep_mem_spechtSubmodule`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.AdjacentSwapStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.AdjacentSwapStep","kind":"def","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L712-L733","doc":"**An admissible adjacent-swap step between standard tableaux**, recorded at the level of\ntheir content vectors (all the seminormal transport needs).  `T'` is obtained from `T` by an\nadjacent swap `(a, b)` (`b = a + 1`) when: the content vectors of `T'` and `T` agree away from\n`{a, b}` and are swapped at `{a, b}`; and the content gap `d = c_T(b) − c_T(a)` satisfies\n`d ≠ 0` and `d² ≠ 1`.  The two gap conditions are the classical admissibility: for a standard\ntableau, consecutive labels never sit on the same diagonal (`d ≠ 0`), and `|d| = 1` exactly when\nthey are row- or column-adjacent — the case in which the swapped filling is *not* standard.  So\nan `AdjacentSwapStep` is precisely \"swap `a, a+1` in `T`, landing on another standard tableau\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv","kind":"def","line":700,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L700-L710","doc":"**The cell-bijection of a standard tableau (constructed sorry-free).** For a standard Young\ntableau `T` of shape `μ`, the bijection `Fin (nOf μ) ≃ μ.cells` reading label `k` to the unique\ncell of `μ` holding `k`.  This is **brick 4's** `SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau`: the inverse of\nthe cell→label map `cellLabel T` (an injection between two finite types of equal cardinality\n`μ.cells.card = μ.card = nOf μ`, hence a bijection — `cellLabel_bijective`).  Carrying it here lets\nus *construct* the `cellOf` field of a `SeminormalVector` explicitly, so the only OV input that\nremains in `jucysMurphy_eigenvalue` is the seminormal eigenvector itself (not its indexing\nbijection).  No `sorry`, no `ℝ`, no `k`-dependence (it is tableau data only). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_smul_seminormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_smul_seminormal","kind":"theorem","line":682,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L682-L698","doc":"**`C₂` acts on a seminormal vector by `contentSqSum μ`.** The central element\n`C₂ = ∑_k X_k²` acts on the seminormal vector `sv.v` by the scalar `contentSqSum μ`.\n\nSorry-free.  The proof distributes `ρ(C₂) = ρ(∑_k X_k²) = ∑_k ρ(X_k²)` (via `map_sum` and\n`LinearMap.sum_apply`), evaluates each summand by `jucysMurphy_sq_smul_seminormal`\n(`= c(cellOf k)² • v`), pulls the `zsmul` out of the sum (`Finset.sum_smul` / `Finset.sum_zsmul`),\nand collapses `∑_k c(cellOf k)² = contentSqSum μ` by `contentSqSum_eq_sum_over_labels` along the\nbijection `sv.cellOf`.  This is the sorry-free core of the punchline; the only remaining OV input\n(the *spanning* of `S^λ` by such vectors) is isolated in `seminormalVectors_span`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_sq_smul_seminormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_sq_smul_seminormal","kind":"theorem","line":669,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L669-L680","doc":"**Each JM square acts on a seminormal vector by the content square.** From the seminormal\neigenproperty `X_s · v = c(cellOf s) • v`, the square `X_s² = X_s ∘ X_s` acts by `c(cellOf s)² • v`.\nSorry-free; the only inputs are `Representation.asAlgebraHom` being an algebra hom (so `map_pow`\nsends `X_s²` to `(ρ X_s)²`) and the `zsmul` square computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_eq_sum_over_labels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_eq_sum_over_labels","kind":"theorem","line":658,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L658-L667","doc":"**Content-square sum over labels = over cells.** For any bijection `e : Fin (nOf μ) ≃ μ.cells`,\nthe sum of `cellContent (e s)²` over the labels `s` equals `contentSqSum μ = ∑_{c∈μ.cells} c(c)²`.\nA pure reindexing of a finite sum along the bijection (`Finset.sum_attach` + `Fintype.sum_equiv`);\n**no `sorry`, no `ℝ`** — integer arithmetic over `ℤ` (§7c-clean).  This is the \"content-sum\narithmetic\" leg of the punchline: it turns the JM-eigenvalue sum into the keystone's `ω = Σc²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.isEig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.isEig","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L654-L654","doc":"**Seminormal eigenproperty.** Each `X_k` acts on `v` by the scalar\n`cellContent (cellOf k)` (an integer, via `zsmul`).  This is the defining diagonality of the\nGZ basis; its *existence* (a full GZ basis with this property) is the OV theorem stubbed in\n`jucysMurphy_eigenvalue`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.cellOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.cellOf","kind":"def","line":649,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L649-L649","doc":"The **bijection** `Fin (nOf μ) ≃ μ.cells` induced by the tableau `T`: label `k ↦` the cell\nof `μ` carrying `k`.  Bijective because a standard tableau is a bijection labels ↔ cells (brick 1's\n`inj_on` + the card identity `μ.cells.card = μ.card = nOf μ`).  Carrying the bijection (rather than\na bare function) is what lets the content-square sum over labels collapse to `contentSqSum μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.nz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.nz","kind":"theorem","line":644,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L644-L644","doc":"It is nonzero (so \"eigenvector\" is non-vacuous). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.mem","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L642-L642","doc":"It lies in the Specht submodule `S^λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.v","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.v","kind":"def","line":640,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L640-L640","doc":"The seminormal vector itself, an element of the ambient permutation module `M^λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.T","kind":"def","line":638,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L638-L638","doc":"The standard Young tableau indexing this GZ basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector.mk","kind":"ctor","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L636-L636","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.SeminormalVector","kind":"structure","line":612,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L612-L656","doc":"A **seminormal (Gelfand–Zetlin) eigenvector** of the Specht module `S^λ`, packaged abstractly\nso that the eigenvalue theorem can be stated at the level of brick 2's `Specht.Mtab.rep` without\nfirst constructing the whole GZ basis (which is itself the content of the OV theorem).\n\nThe bundle carries:\n* `T` — a standard Young tableau of shape `μ` (brick 1's `StandardYoungTableau`), which indexes the\n  GZ basis vector;\n* `v` — the corresponding seminormal vector, living in the Specht submodule `S^λ ≤ M^λ`;\n* `nz` — non-triviality (`v ≠ 0`), so \"eigenvector\" is meaningful;\n* `cellOf` — the **bijection** `Fin (nOf μ) ≃ μ.cells` that `T` induces, reading label `k` to the\n  cell of `μ` holding `k`.  This is a bijection because a standard tableau fills the `nOf μ = μ.card`\n  cells with the labels `0, …, nOf μ − 1` exactly once (brick 1's `StandardYoungTableau.inj_on`);\n  packaging it as an `Equiv` is the faithful form of \"the cell holding label `k`\", and it is what\n  makes the content-square sum over labels equal the content-square sum over cells\n  (`centralC2_smul_seminormal`);\n* `isEig` — the **defining seminormal property**: each `X_k` acts on `v` by the scalar\n  `cellContent (cellOf k)`, i.e. the content of the cell holding label `k` in `T`.  We express\n  the JM action on `M^λ` through `Specht.Mtab.rep` extended to the group algebra\n  (`Representation.asAlgebraHom`), and the integer scalar via `zsmul`.\n\nThis is the *honest* packaging: rather than assert the GZ basis exists (the theorem), we make the\nseminormal-eigenvector data a hypothesis, and `jucysMurphy_eigenvalue` states the consequence that\ncharacterises such a vector.  Replacing this bundle with a constructed GZ basis is exactly the OV\ntheorem (`-- Ref: [vershik-kerov1977]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.rep_mem_spechtSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.rep_mem_spechtSubmodule","kind":"theorem","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L588-L608","doc":"**`S^λ` is invariant under the `S_n`-action** (a subrepresentation): `rep μ σ`\nmaps the Specht submodule into itself.  Span induction over the polytabloid\ngenerators via `rep_polytabloid`.  Sorry-free, generic `[CommRing k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.rep_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.rep_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L562-L586","doc":"**The group action permutes polytabloids**: `rep σ (e_t) = e_{σ·t}`.  Reindex the\ncolumn-stabilizer sum along the conjugation `π ↦ σπσ⁻¹` (`colStabConj`); signs are\nconjugation-invariant and `(σπσ⁻¹)·(σ·t) = σ·(π·t)`.  Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_involution_eigenvector_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_involution_eigenvector_ne","kind":"theorem","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L500-L532","doc":"**The 2×2 seminormal block, non-vanishing half.** If `S² = 1`, `v ≠ 0`, and\n`(cb − ca)² ≠ 1`, then `w = S v − (cb − ca)⁻¹ • v ≠ 0`: from `w = 0` the vector `v`\nwould be an `S`-eigenvector with eigenvalue `r = (cb − ca)⁻¹`, forcing `r² = 1` by the\ninvolution — i.e. `(cb − ca)² = 1` (with the degenerate `cb = ca` giving `r = 0`,\n`r² = 0 ≠ 1`, also excluded).  Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_conj_fix_eigenvector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_conj_fix_eigenvector","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L482-L498","doc":"**The 2×2 seminormal block, fixed-operator half.** An operator `C` fixed by the\nconjugation (`S·C·S = C`, `S² = 1`) commutes with `S`, so it keeps its eigenvalue on\n`w = S v − r • v` for any shift `r`.  Sorry-free, generic `[CommRing k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_conj_shift_eigenvector_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.end_conj_shift_eigenvector_pair","kind":"theorem","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L441-L480","doc":"**The 2×2 seminormal block, eigenvalue-swap half.** If `S² = 1`, `S·A·S = B − S`\n(the Jucys–Murphy recursion, abstractly), and `v` is an `A`-eigenvector with value `ca`\nand a `B`-eigenvector with value `cb ≠ ca`, then `w = S v − (cb − ca)⁻¹ • v` is an\n`A`-eigenvector with value `cb` and a `B`-eigenvector with value `ca` (the swapped pair).\nSorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.pair_shift_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.pair_shift_comm","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L408-L429","doc":"Abstract ring fact: if `s² = 1` and `s·Y·s = Z − s`, then `s` commutes with `Y² + Z²`.\nThe pure noncommutative-ring core of the Jucys–Murphy centrality argument: from the\nhypotheses, `s·Y = Z·s − 1` and `s·Z = Y·s + 1`, and the cross terms cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.conj_jucysMurphy_other","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.conj_jucysMurphy_other","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L372-L406","doc":"**The other Jucys–Murphy elements are fixed** by conjugation with an adjacent swap:\n`s·X_m·s = X_m` for `m ∉ {a, b}` — the swap permutes the index set `{j : j < m}`.\nSorry-free, generic `[CommRing k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.conj_jucysMurphy_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.conj_jucysMurphy_self","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L351-L370","doc":"**The Jucys–Murphy recursion (algebra form).** `s·X_a·s = X_b − s` for the adjacent swap\n`s = (a b)`, `b = a + 1`: conjugation sends each `(j a)` (`j < a`) to `(j b)`, and\n`X_b = ∑_{j<a} (j b) + (a b)`.  Sorry-free, generic `[CommRing k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_commute","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L314-L328","doc":"**Commutativity of the Gelfand–Zetlin algebra.** The Jucys–Murphy elements pairwise commute:\nthey generate a maximal commutative (Gelfand–Zetlin) subalgebra of `k[S_n]`.  This is the\nstructural fact underlying the simultaneous-eigenbasis (seminormal) construction.  Proved\nsorry-free by Jucys's classical computation (see `jm_commute_lt`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_coeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_coeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L202-L208","doc":"The identity coefficient of the brick-5 `C₂` is `binom(n,2)` — re-exported from the merged\nℂ-free core (`JucysMurphyCoeff.centralC2_coeff_one`), through the definitional equality above.\nSorry-free.  (A non-vacuous sanity check that the JM packaging is wired to the proved coefficient\nidentity; the *eigenvalue* form is the deep theorem stubbed below.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_eq_sum_jucysMurphy_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_eq_sum_jucysMurphy_sq","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L196-L200","doc":"The brick-5 `centralC2` (built from `jucysMurphy`) coincides with the established\n`QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2` used by the keystone's trace computation — they unfold\nto the same `MonoidAlgebra` element.  Sorry-free: pure `rfl` on the two definitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L189-L194","doc":"The Jucys–Murphy **central element** `C₂ = ∑_k X_k²` of `k[S_n]`, packaged directly from the\n`jucysMurphy` elements.  By construction this is *definitionally equal* to\n`QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2 n` (the two inner sums coincide), recorded in\n`centralC2_eq_sum_jucysMurphy_sq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L181-L185","doc":"`contentSqSum` is always nonnegative (a sum of integer squares).  This is a statement about\nthe **integers** (`Int.le`), not an archimedean fact about `k` — it lives entirely in `ℤ`, so it\nis §7c-clean.  Useful downstream when reading `ω` as a magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum_bot","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L177-L179","doc":"The empty diagram has content-square sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.contentSqSum","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L171-L175","doc":"The **content-square sum** `ω_λ = ∑_{c∈λ} c(c)²` of a Young diagram, as an integer.  This is\nthe scalar by which the JM central element `C₂ = ∑_k X_k²` acts on the Specht module `S^λ`\n(`centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum`), i.e. the `ω = Σc²` field carried by the keystone's\n`SnWedderburnSpectralData`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent_diag","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L167-L169","doc":"The diagonal cells `(i, i)` have content `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent_apply","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellContent","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L160-L163","doc":"The **content** of a cell `c = (i, j)` of a Young diagram: `c(i,j) = j − i` (column minus row),\nas an integer.  Constant on diagonals; the eigenvalue by which the JM element `X_k` acts on a\nseminormal vector whose strand `k` sits in cell `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_succ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_succ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L137-L156","doc":"On `Fin (n+2)` (where the index `1` genuinely exists), `X_1 = (0 1) = single (swap 0 1) 1`:\nthe only strand below `1` is `0`. A second sorry-free sanity check that the definition picks up\nexactly the strands below the index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_zero","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L126-L135","doc":"`X_0 = 0`: the sum over `j < 0` is empty (no strand sits below the first one). The easy\nsorry-free anchor for the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphy.lean#L116-L124","doc":"The **Jucys–Murphy element** `X_i = ∑_{j < i} (j i)` of `k[S_n] = MonoidAlgebra k (Perm (Fin n))`:\nthe sum of the transpositions `(j i)` for every strand `j` below `i`, each weighted `1`.\n\nThe filter `j.val < i.val` is the order on the **index type** `Fin n` (the strands), not an order\non the ring `k` (§7c-clean).  This is *definitionally* the inner summand of\n`QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2`, so `∑ k, (jucysMurphy n k)^2` unfolds to that\nestablished central element (see `centralC2_eq_sum_jucysMurphy_sq`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}